          },
          {
            "id": 2831569,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Unusually for his time, he didn't care whether his guests were rich or poor as long as they had talent. Big houses like Oniton had dozens of servants until the nineteen twenties or thirties, and we've tried to show what their working lives were like. Photographs, of course, don't give much of an idea. So instead, as you go round the house, you'll see volunteers dressed up as nineteenth century servants going about their work. They'll explain what they're doing and tell you their recipes or what tools they're using.",
