          {
            "id": 2831779,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "We'll also be going into the farm that's part of the estate where there's plenty to do. Most of the buildings date from the eighteenth century, so you can really step back into an agricultural past. Until recently, the dairy was where milk from the cows was turned into cheese. It's now the place to go for lunch or afternoon tea or just a cup of coffee and a slice of homemade cake. The big stone building that dominates the farm is the large barn, and in here is our collection of agricultural tools.",
